<p>Israeli officials said the security cabinet met on April 15 to discuss a possible ceasefire in Lebanon, even as Israel kept striking Hezbollah positions in southern Lebanon. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said it was still too early to know how the matter would end. The diplomatic opening followed rare direct talks between Israeli and Lebanese envoys in Washington on April 14. The United States called those talks productive and described them as the start of direct negotiations between the two countries after more than three decades without official meetings. The talks open a notable diplomatic channel in a conflict that has escalated for more than five weeks and that several reports tie to the broader U.S.-Israeli confrontation with Iran, as well as parallel U.S.-Iran diplomacy. Still, the fighting has not paused. Israeli operations remained focused on areas including Bint Jbeil, which Netanyahu described as a Hezbollah stronghold, and U.S. reporting said Washington welcomed the negotiations but did not publicly press Israel to halt strikes or withdraw from Lebanese territory.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DTxsV54lNjkhCtu3Mh2yqychEXHSWHeP0LyJpG1uWDordxMVRwUZ8QwAQkvAEbYwXVtQWTMrTOv3W837mmgBaJ5205123Zqa_mmF1Z2zyEAna7-ELDTt0DsR1YXqLhN7FNJ5KHCWQboOeRoaep5bttqB_IpdA-Gh4gsat8WrYXHdwYcsbhkd2zBzjxPzLt-9HDpkwhloExQ1ow' alt='Israeli and Lebanese envoys take part in U.S.-mediated direct talks in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Israeli envoy&#x27;s message: After the Washington talks, Israel&#x27;s U.S. ambassador Yechiel Leiter said the delegations agreed that &quot;the evil of Hezbollah must be eradicated&quot;.</li><li>Lebanese political rift: Hezbollah and allied voices said the direct talks with Israel widened a national divide in Lebanon, underscoring that the movement does not see the bilateral track as speaking for it.</li><li>Military planning: Even as officials weighed ceasefire options, Israel&#x27;s top general approved plans to continue attacks in both Lebanon and Iran.</li><li>No immediate breakthrough: The Washington meeting ended with encouraging language and talk of further contacts, but the sides made no firm commitments.</li><li>Battlefield toll: Lebanon&#x27;s health ministry said Israeli attacks had killed at least 2,124 people in six weeks, including 168 children and 88 health workers, while Israel said 13 soldiers and at least two Israeli civilians had been killed.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Israel&#x27;s goals matched those of the United States and that Israel was prepared for any scenario as ceasefire discussions unfolded. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-us-goals-identical-prepared-for-any-scenario-netanyahu/article70866591.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Lebanese government: Lebanese envoy Nada Hamadeh Moawad said she used the Washington talks to stress Lebanon&#x27;s territorial integrity and state sovereignty, and to call for a ceasefire. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>The Week</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: Hezbollah signaled it could accept a ceasefire if regional diplomacy succeeds, but also said it would not abide by arrangements produced by direct Israel-Lebanon negotiations. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3350220/israeli-security-cabinet-discuss-possible-lebanon-ceasefire-senior-official'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>United States: Secretary of State Marco Rubio mediated more than two hours of talks that ended with an agreement to open a direct negotiation channel between Israeli and Lebanese envoys. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-lebanon-agree-to-direct-negotiations-after-productive-talks-us/article70863576.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>United Nations: U.N. Secretary-General António Guterres said both Hezbollah and Israel had contributed to destabilizing Lebanon&#x27;s government. (<a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>The Week</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israeli-military-continues-to-strike-hezbollah-amid-lebanon-peace-talks-netanyahu-says'>Israeli military continues to strike Hezbollah amid Lebanon peace talks, Netanyahu says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/hezbollah-hints-at-ceasefire-in-lebanon-israel-says-it-will-ramp-up-attacks-11363255#publisher=newsstand'>Hezbollah Hints At Ceasefire In Lebanon, Israel To Ramp Up Attacks</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3350220/israeli-security-cabinet-discuss-possible-lebanon-ceasefire-senior-official'>Israeli security cabinet to discuss possible Lebanon ceasefire: senior official</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/40218940-4f0f-4aee-9209-2fb713eea736'>Lebanon says efforts are under way to reach ceasefire with Israel ‘soon’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/15/iran-war-live-news-us-naval-blockade-strait-of-hormuz-pakistan-peace-talks-middle-east-crisis-latest'>Middle East crisis live: US says Iran talks ‘productive’; Israel continues Lebanon strikes as officials reportedly discuss ceasefire</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-us-goals-identical-prepared-for-any-scenario-netanyahu/article70866591.ece'>Israel, U.S. goals &#x27;identical&#x27;; prepared for any scenario: Netanyahu</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/world-news/israel-lebanon-rare-talks-fighting-war'>Israel and Lebanon hold rare talks as fighting rages</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-ceasefire-preparations-hezbollah.html'>Israel Considering Cease-Fire With Lebanon, Officials Say</a> - nytimes.com</li></ul>